From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: cmdq: return NULL, not -ENOMEM, from a void * function

cmdq_pkt_get_curr_buf_va() returns void * and its failure path returns -ENOMEM:

  drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-cmdq-helper.c:598:32: warning: returning 'int' from a
      function with return type 'void *' makes pointer from integer without a
      cast [-Wint-conversion]

A caller that checked the result would take (void *)-12 for a valid pointer and
dereference it. NULL is the convention for this signature, and nothing in the
tree uses IS_ERR() on it - in fact the symbol is exported and has no in-tree
caller at all, which is presumably how it survived.

The sibling cmdq_pkt_get_curr_buf_pa() returns dma_addr_t, where -ENOMEM is
merely an odd value rather than a bad pointer, and is left alone.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-cmdq-helper.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-cmdq-helper.c
@@ -595,7 +595,7 @@
 
 	if (unlikely(!pkt->avail_buf_size))
 		if (cmdq_pkt_add_cmd_buffer(pkt) < 0)
-			return -ENOMEM;
+			return NULL;
 
 	buf = list_last_entry(&pkt->buf, typeof(*buf), list_entry);
 
